{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1071445-goblin-contract-preview","id":1071445,"title":"Goblin Contract Preview!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-03-31T15:33:49-07:00","id":1071445,"title":"Goblin Contract Preview!","content":"I have to say its beautiful and just what I wanted to see in Changeling. Thanks for making Second Edition the game me and my friends can look forwards to!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1XN7DemY9ZHgxVsiStGXZd_pEVCE-ue5F5X5JSciF8qw/edit\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1XN7DemY9ZHgxVsiStGXZd_pEVCE-ue5F5X5JSciF8qw/edit\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1XN7DemY9ZHgxVsiStGXZd_pEVCE-ue5F5X5JSciF8qw/edit\" target=\"_blank\"> https://docs.google.com/document/d/1XN7DemY9ZHgxVsiStGXZd_pEVCE-ue5F5X5JSciF8qw/edit </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-31T15:44:08-07:00","id":1071452,"title":"","content":"Interesting! Seems like a lot of progress has been made, and is it just me, or are there a lot of lexicon terms in there we haven't seen before? Arcadian Contracts? Regalia? Pupil's Devotion?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-31T15:44:11-07:00","id":1071453,"title":"","content":"My. <br /> Oh my.<br /> <br /> I want more. Goblin Queen. *fans self* Oh goddess. So beautiful.<br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-31T15:48:30-07:00","id":1071455,"title":"","content":"In addition to the Goblin Contracts, we now know we'll be getting rules for generating Hobgoblins. That'll be so useful for me since having to homebrew every opponent was the only thing preventing me from playing Changeling 1e.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1071445-goblin-contract-preview?p=1071452#post1071452\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting! Seems like a lot of progress has been made, and is it just me, or are there a lot of lexicon terms in there we haven't seen before? Arcadian Contracts? Regalia? Pupil's Devotion?</div> </div> </div> </div>Catches seem to have been renamed Loopholes, which seems like an unnecessary change to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 03-31-2017, 06:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-31T15:52:56-07:00","id":1071457,"title":"","content":"doublepost.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-31T16:04:16-07:00","id":1071466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1071445-goblin-contract-preview?p=1071452#post1071452\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">is it just me, or are there a lot of lexicon terms in there we haven't seen before? Arcadian Contracts? Regalia? Pupil's Devotion?</div> </div> </div> </div> It sounds like just formal names for things. Arcadian Contracts are probably standard Contracts (especially since Contracts were originally said to be made by the Gentry back in 1e), and then we have Goblin Contracts and Court Contracts. Regalia is probably just another name for seeming-affinity clauses while Pupil's Devotion is how you buy said affinity clauses when not that seeming. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-31T16:08:36-07:00","id":1071471,"title":"","content":"It looks interesting. I am wondering how this fits in with what we've seen so far, or if they really did scrap everything and start from scratch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10769-llegume","name":"LLegume","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-31T16:22:50-07:00","id":1071482,"title":"","content":"Other things of note - Goblin Luck is basically 1e's Trading Luck for Fate, and Mantle Mask is already a goblin contract from 1e's Dancer in the Dusk. So, we can basically do a direct trade of 1e gob contracts for 2e's, it seems. At pretty much the same level, too. <br /> <br /> Goblins might be able to produce the power behind Contracts, which makes me wonder if a Goblin Queen could power Goblin Contracts. Or even goblin vows.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-31T16:26:15-07:00","id":1071484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1071445-goblin-contract-preview?p=1071455#post1071455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In addition to the Goblin Contracts, we now know we'll be getting rules for generating Hobgoblins. That'll be so useful for me since having to homebrew every opponent was the only thing preventing me from playing Changeling 1e.<br /> <br /> <br /> Catches seem to have been renamed Loopholes, which seems like an unnecessary change to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think its a good change. Catch always seemed to be a strange term to me for what it meant in the game. I agree that Hobgoblin generation rules is a very welcome addition though!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-31T16:29:59-07:00","id":1071486,"title":"","content":"Can you still play with a character after his goblinization?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-31T16:31:49-07:00","id":1071488,"title":"","content":"Why not? They're Clairty 5, and nothing about the character is utterly inhuman, and the Hedge is still part-reality, not full reality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-31T16:32:06-07:00","id":1071489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LLegume</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1071445-goblin-contract-preview?p=1071471#post1071471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It looks interesting. I am wondering how this fits in with what we've seen so far, or if they really did scrap everything and start from scratch.</div> </div> </div> </div>The flavour of goblin contracts is the same as from the earlier contract previews, and differences it has with previous rules seems to be:<ul><li>It lacks seeming benefit, which might be limited to goblin contracts or apply to all contracts now.</li> <li>Wording changes like giving a specific name to standard contracts (Arcadian Contracts) which seems to be so readers know whether something applies to Contracts in general or specifically to the default types of contracts.</li> <li>Renaming things like catches to loopholes.</li> <li>It sounds like there is some way to make contracts cheaper called Regalia, not sure if it is linked to courts, entitlements, or seemings.</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-31T17:06:52-07:00","id":1071508,"title":"","content":"Wa-how. I love this. <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZvyNOg4jSRg\" target=\"_blank\">I can finally live my dream!</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-31T17:26:40-07:00","id":1071516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1071445-goblin-contract-preview?p=1071484#post1071484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think its a good change. Catch always seemed to be a strange term to me for what it meant in the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I agree. Catch never quite made sense. Loophole is a better word for what it's going for.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-31T18:03:40-07:00","id":1071522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1071445-goblin-contract-preview?p=1071488#post1071488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why not? They're Clairty 5, and nothing about the character is utterly inhuman, and the Hedge is still part-reality, not full reality.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Also, you become a Goblin Monarch at Clarity 5....and <i>you don't develop a cap by being one</i>.<br /> <br /> There is nothing in the world, minus the fact that the Hedge provokes a lot of Breaking Points, that prevents a goblin-changeling from having high Clarity. In fact, I would argue that a goblin Lost has embraced Clarity; the Hedge is a world of madness and dreams, but it's also a place you can't dwell in without developing a little empathy, given what Thorns are made of. The many goblin kingdoms of the Hedge may be mad, but they aren't heartless like the Gentry. You speak with the Goblin Queen, you speak with someone who may actually care about the spirit of a deal as well as the letter.<br /> <br /> Welcome to your new house, little king. Now, how will you make it a home?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-31T19:13:52-07:00","id":1071546,"title":"","content":"I find very distinct and fascinating the implication that Goblins may be as defined by <i>debt</i> as the true denizens of arcadia are by stories and oaths. Food for thought, and the previewed mechanics make Goblin Contracts seem like a very dangerous and interesting arrangement.<br /> <br /> The lexicon change caught me by surprise but it doesn't seem bad. Distinguishing 'regular' contracts from Goblin Contracts by calling them Arcadian and renaming Catch to Loophole are more of a plain language shift, and the former even brings some pertinent implications.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-31T19:22:11-07:00","id":1071551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1071445-goblin-contract-preview?p=1071486#post1071486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you still play with a character after his goblinization?</div> </div> </div> </div>Absolutely!<br /> <br /> As for Regalia, they're the categories for Arcadian Contracts. Sword for strength, Shield for defense, Crown for leadership, Jewels for manipulation and temptation, Mirror for perception and self-transformation, and Steed for movement. Each seeming has a favored Regalia, and a player chooses a second favored Regalia for her character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-31T20:06:28-07:00","id":1071567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1071445-goblin-contract-preview?p=1071551#post1071551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Absolutely!<br /> <br /> As for Regalia, they're the categories for Arcadian Contracts. Sword for strength, Shield for defense, Crown for leadership, Jewels for manipulation and temptation, Mirror for perception and self-transformation, and Steed for movement. Each seeming has a favored Regalia, and a player chooses a second favored Regalia for her character.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Whoa. If Arcadian Contracts are...all Contracts not Goblin, that's a pretty major change from the playtest.<br /> <br /> It's fairer (no more 'no special seeming for you!' problem-how not all Contracts give all bonuses), but I want to make clear; I am right in thinking that Arcadian Contracts are &quot;normal&quot; Contracts, right?<br /> <br /> And if so, all Seeming bonuses should be renamed for the Seeming that favors that Regalia, yes? (Going by the names, I assume Ogres are Sword, Fairest are Crown, Steed is Beasts, Mirror is Wizened, but the others...don't see it easily).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-31T20:07:28-07:00","id":1071568,"title":"","content":"Huh. Neat. Sounds like stuff has changed a fair bit since the playtestable chunks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-31T20:33:37-07:00","id":1071586,"title":"","content":"You'll see a lot of the same Contract powers as in the earlier docs, but organized differently. Arcadian Contracts are the biggest group of Contracts, distinct from Court Contracts and Goblin Contracts. We restructured them for a number of reasons, but one of the big ones was to ease character creation. The implications of the word &quot;Arcadian&quot; are deliberate, but there's more to Arcadia than just Gentry....<br /> <br /> There are still seeming benefits for Contracts. One of those benefits is always for the seeming that favors that Regalia.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":2,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","user":"Rose Bailey","date":". 03-31-2017, 11:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-31T22:06:54-07:00","id":1071616,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1071445-goblin-contract-preview?p=1071551#post1071551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for Regalia, they're the categories for Arcadian Contracts. Sword for strength, Shield for defense, Crown for leadership, Jewels for manipulation and temptation, Mirror for perception and self-transformation, and Steed for movement. Each seeming has a favored Regalia, and a player chooses a second favored Regalia for her character.</div> </div> </div> </div>Abit disappointed because it means characters in a seeming might be less varied, but it does sound like a considerably easier format from a design standpoint.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 04-01-2017, 01:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-31T23:28:52-07:00","id":1071631,"title":"","content":"I must say- Goblin Contracts does look like a very fun mechanics, as presented here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-31T23:39:22-07:00","id":1071633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1071445-goblin-contract-preview?p=1071551#post1071551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Absolutely!<br /> <br /> As for Regalia, they're the categories for Arcadian Contracts. Sword for strength, Shield for defense, Crown for leadership, Jewels for manipulation and temptation, Mirror for perception and self-transformation, and Steed for movement. Each seeming has a favored Regalia, and a player chooses a second favored Regalia for her character.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does this mean Regalia influences what Seeming Clauses your character gets by default? Or does that mean you have to pay more Experience to purchase the Contract from a non-favored Regalia?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-01T01:28:05-07:00","id":1071654,"title":"","content":"Shouldn't exist also a mechanic to allow the changeling to work out his debt, rather than waiting to the wrath of the GM?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-01T04:52:07-07:00","id":1071677,"title":"","content":"The default Contracts have always been made by the Gentry, going back to 1e core. It wasn't until Equinox Road that non-Gentry ever struck any... So, Arcadian Contracts is pretty much just a formalization of that old idea. So, Arcadian Contracts are by the True Fae (and other such arcadian denizens), the Goblin Contracts by the Hedge, and Court Contracts by the fae of Ironside. Seems pretty logical.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Sword for strength, Shield for defense, Crown for leadership, Jewels for manipulation and temptation, Mirror for perception and self-transformation, and Steed for movement. </div> </div> </div>Ogres being swords, Fairest being crowns, Beasts being Steed does seem fairly obvious - not only the abilities but the names are pretty clear links. The other three aren't as clear - I'm thinking that Jewels will be Darkling (subtlty and manipulation of senses for invisibility), Mirror for Elemental (self-transformation into an element is a thing, after all) and that would leave Shield for Wizened. Not really sure how the wizened themes of artifice is really lending to &quot;defense&quot; but then, I wouldn't put perception and self-transformation, strength, leadership, temptation nor movement as their affinity either. Honestly, &quot;Defense&quot; is a hard one, since the closest thing to defense contracts are Separation / phantom glory / red rage of revenge. And those are traditionally Fairest / Ogre abilties. Or Elemental, with Cloak of the Elements. Not really wizened. I wonder how that's going to work.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm not really sure how I feel about these affinities being so different from seeming-themed feels. 1e Fang and Talon, for instance, has self-transformation, movement, and leading animals at least. That's three Regalia at least. Contracts of Darkness had... well, that was always an odd grab bag of fear manipulation and movement. I feel like we're stepping away from having anything related to Seemings here. I mean, I found it pretty awesome that Boon of the Scuttling Spider now had a Beast clause for making webbing. That doesn't feel like a thing as much.<br /> <br /> I mean, it makes sense. If the vast majority of Contracts originated without Changelings or their Seemings, then why should Seemings get benefits? And the Regalia themes do tie into the existing Seemings' Escapes. Fairest lead others. Thus, crown. Ogres relied on strength (sword). Beasts ran away (steed). Darklings used trickery and underhanded tactics (jewels). Elementals transformed into raw elements and escaped that way (mirror). And Wizened protected the core of their humanity by building a robot body around it (shield). Well, not necessarily a robot, since it could be non-robot parts, but you get the idea. Built a shield around their heart, &quot;the choice to devote herself to the thing that brings safety, comfort, and praise.&quot; So, all these new Regilia logically flow from the Seemings and how they escape. It all makes sense that way.<br /> <br /> However, it feels a step removed from what it used to be. I think we're going to be a bit more difficult filling in old concepts with a new way to have these contracts work. Just because you're an elemental doesn't mean you'll have an affinity for everything raw elements anymore. Wizened won't automatically be artificers. And so on. Not sure how I feel about it at the moment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 04-01-2017, 07:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-01T05:17:54-07:00","id":1071680,"title":"","content":"Oh, so if you abuse them, you become a Goblin?<br /> <br /> Not sure if that's a good thing or not. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1071445-goblin-contract-preview?p=1071486#post1071486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you still play with a character after his goblinization?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I would imagine so, since it talks about how to reverse the process. It just becomes harder to act outside the Hedge, depending on how far gone you are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 04-01-2017, 08:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-01T08:57:58-07:00","id":1071726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1071445-goblin-contract-preview?p=1071586#post1071586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You'll see a lot of the same Contract powers as in the earlier docs, but organized differently. Arcadian Contracts are the biggest group of Contracts, distinct from Court Contracts and Goblin Contracts. We restructured them for a number of reasons, but one of the big ones was to ease character creation. The implications of the word &quot;Arcadian&quot; are deliberate, but there's more to Arcadia than just Gentry....<br /> <br /> There are still seeming benefits for Contracts. One of those benefits is always for the seeming that favors that Regalia.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a big relief to me. I really liked the playtest style of having the seeming affinity perks and I'm glad the rewrite didn't change that completely. The new organization style seems really cool from what you're saying here and I'm looking forward to seeing an updated Contracts section spoiled at some point? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Is there going to be a change to XP costs for contracts or still 1xp/dot?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10769-llegume","name":"LLegume","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-01T09:25:03-07:00","id":1071732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1071445-goblin-contract-preview?p=1071677#post1071677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[...]<br /> <br /> However, it feels a step removed from what it used to be. I think we're going to be a bit more difficult filling in old concepts with a new way to have these contracts work. Just because you're an elemental doesn't mean you'll have an affinity for everything raw elements anymore. Wizened won't automatically be artificers. And so on. Not sure how I feel about it at the moment.</div> </div> </div> </div>A sensible analysis of how the new terminology and its symbolism matches up to what we saw before, though there are some points that feel a bit ambiguous still. The Seeming bonuses actually felt very on point to me before because they seemed to be tied with the relation between a Changeling's Kith and their Seeming.<br /> <br /> With Kith being what Gentry made you into and the story they gave you, and Seeming being how you took back agency and made that story your own, the bonuses were like <i>your uniquely human twist on the Contracts signed by the True Fae</i>. Which would make Seeming bonuses exclusive to Changelings. This was never really <i>said</i>, but it seemed like a significant implication that reinforced the differences between the lords of arcadia and their victims, and I was hoping the final text would support that.<br /> <br /> The breaking of a direct match between the bonuses and the Seeming concepts feels like it opens holes in the expected affinities of each to certain contracts to me too, but I don't know! Curious if we'll be able to see something about how the setup has changed soon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-01T10:29:09-07:00","id":1071749,"title":"","content":"Regalia also opens things up for the Grimm and other Seemings. And maybe in random, non-fixed ways. Rewrite your Regalia between sessions! Could be interesting<br /> <br /> <br /> And Remember we get two affinities - one that is likely given by the Gentry for the Loyalists, then you stole a second during escape. So, expect Loyalists with Regalia now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-01T11:39:03-07:00","id":1071763,"title":"","content":"Hrm, I don't think that really changes much, all things considered, but I'm interested in the implications of Regalia. Realize now I misunderstood something on my first read, because Bailey said there <i>are still</i> seeming benefits for contracts (which relieves some worries about them not following quite as naturally anymore) and Regalia are a categorization change.<br /> <br /> So are basic Contracts still going to be individual powers rated 1-5 with cost in Experiences equal to their rating, or do <i>favored</i> categories imply a cost difference? I would be a little sad if it's the latter, because the paradigm from the original preview made things more fun for everyone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 04-01-2017, 02:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-01T11:50:27-07:00","id":1071772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1071445-goblin-contract-preview?p=1071466#post1071466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> It sounds like just formal names for things. Arcadian Contracts are probably standard Contracts (especially since Contracts were originally said to be made by the Gentry back in 1e), and then we have Goblin Contracts and Court Contracts. Regalia is probably just another name for seeming-affinity clauses while Pupil's Devotion is how you buy said affinity clauses when not that seeming. </div> </div> </div> </div> That actually makes a lot of sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-01T12:36:23-07:00","id":1071786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1071445-goblin-contract-preview?p=1071654#post1071654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shouldn't exist also a mechanic to allow the changeling to work out his debt, rather than waiting to the wrath of the GM?</div> </div> </div> </div> One of the Resolutions for Hedge Denizen hints at this, but it's not clear if you can just go to the Goblin and work off your debt or make a trade or whatever. <br /> <br /> It's also an interesting way to organize things. Arcadian Contracts are the main contracts, contracts made by the inhabitants of Arcadia, and tied to Arcadia. The new name for Universal Contracts. <br /> <br /> Goblin Contracts are with Goblins and tied to the Hedge. <br /> <br /> Court Contracts are likely tied to Ironside.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-01T13:23:05-07:00","id":1071799,"title":"","content":"Is it possible that some Contracts might have multiple Regalia?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-01T14:06:39-07:00","id":1071806,"title":"","content":"When I remembered it was April 1st I thought it was an April fools joke, the obvious Labyrinth tie in, then I saw Frost Giant Butt Warriors and realized that the Goblin Contracts connection to the movie Labyrinth was just a friendly homage to the movie (love that movie).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-01T14:17:27-07:00","id":1071811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1071445-goblin-contract-preview?p=1071551#post1071551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Absolutely!<br /> <br /> As for Regalia, they're the categories for Arcadian Contracts. Sword for strength, Shield for defense, Crown for leadership, Jewels for manipulation and temptation, Mirror for perception and self-transformation, and Steed for movement. Each seeming has a favored Regalia, and a player chooses a second favored Regalia for her character.</div> </div> </div> </div> If I had to guess Sword = Orges, Crown = Fairest, Steed = Beast, Shield = Elemental, Mirror = Wizen, Jewels = Darkling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-01T14:34:08-07:00","id":1071815,"title":"","content":"The only worry I have is that the wrong GM with this system could be...well, vindictive with it. They may deliberately wait until a player accrues 10 Goblin Debt, simply to lay a condition that makes things harder all of a sudden, such as the Blind condition on a Changeling trying to escape a building, or completely decimate a player's dice pool at a key moment just to extend the plot. They may outright refuse to call in the debt so it rolls over and the player gets Hedge Denizen without them meaning to.<br /> <br /> Of course, a player shouldn't have to worry about that kind of problem with their GM, and ideally players and GMs would have enough trust, respect and or a system in place so that debt can be used constructively. A vindictive GM would have plenty of other methods of messing with players as well outside of this system, too, particularly since players need to actively buy into Goblin Contracts before they can be affected by the debt. It's just...worrying me a lot more than it should.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-01T14:51:30-07:00","id":1071817,"title":"","content":"Question: is the Loophole just the Catch, or does it offer a way to get out of the Goblin Debt instead/as well? Because it does look like the old Goblin Contract drawback.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 04-01-2017, 05:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-01T14:51:36-07:00","id":1071818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1071445-goblin-contract-preview?p=1071815#post1071815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only worry I have is that the wrong GM with this system could be...well, vindictive with it. They may deliberately wait until a player accrues 10 Goblin Debt, simply to lay a condition that makes things harder all of a sudden, such as the Blind condition on a Changeling trying to escape a building, or completely decimate a player's dice pool at a key moment just to extend the plot. They may outright refuse to call in the debt so it rolls over and the player gets Hedge Denizen without them meaning to.<br /> <br /> Of course, a player shouldn't have to worry about that kind of problem with their GM, and ideally players and GMs would have enough trust, respect and or a system in place so that debt can be used constructively. A vindictive GM would have plenty of other methods of messing with players as well outside of this system, too, particularly since players need to actively buy into Goblin Contracts before they can be affected by the debt. It's just...worrying me a lot more than it should.</div> </div> </div> </div>A system cannot answer for a bad GM. Nothing can be done in terms of the system design to answer the sheer freedom a vindictive GM has to fuck over the players.<br /> <br /> With that in mind, it's better to build an evocative system and trust players to not play with assholes rather than try and answer the unanswerable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-01T15:05:19-07:00","id":1071821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1071445-goblin-contract-preview?p=1071818#post1071818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A system cannot answer for a bad GM. Nothing can be done in terms of the system design to answer the sheer freedom a vindictive GM has to fuck over the players.<br /> <br /> With that in mind, it's better to build an evocative system and trust players to not play with assholes rather than try and answer the unanswerable.</div> </div> </div> </div>Completely fair point.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-01T18:05:36-07:00","id":1071854,"title":"","content":"And to be fair, a player who hits 10 Debt is going to do so expecting either 1) to hit Hedge Denizen, or 2) to get smacked with a large debt on purpose because of plot hooks. I'm more than half tempted to buy up a Goblin Vow for my PC right now, and aim for Goblin Queen. I'd become a goblin faster than the vendictive ST could think to slap me with the debt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-01T18:50:14-07:00","id":1071861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1071445-goblin-contract-preview?p=1071817#post1071817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question: is the Loophole just the Catch, or does it offer a way to get out of the Goblin Debt instead/as well? Because it does look like the old Goblin Contract drawback.</div> </div> </div> </div> Excellent question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-01T19:32:11-07:00","id":1071869,"title":"","content":"I just came back from seeing Power Rangers, and I just realized:<br /> <br /> The Debt system is an excellent way to RP becoming a Sentai or Magical Girls villain.<br /> <br /> Seriously, you have the Goblin Queen who cannot fight the heroes directly that often, her loyal, Condition-mandated lieutenants, and the various goblins she trawls up from the Hedge as the monsters of the week. There's even a system for calling them into being if the Queen figures out how to birth Incubi from the dreams of her victims. <br /> <br /> Going away from my April Fool's mandated idea, does anyone want to play a game where all the players are Goblin Monarchs? Sort of like an alliance between them to form a sort of Hedge Empire and attempt to conquer/liberate/whatever a city?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-01T19:37:27-07:00","id":1071872,"title":"","content":"I just realized that the Goblin Queen condition allows Changelings to create new Changelings. <br /> <br /> Character A is careless with his goblin debt and gains the Hedge Denizen Condition and in time trades it in for Goblin Queen. <br /> <br /> Character A gets rid of it by finding a human child and makes them Goblin Queen. <br /> <br /> The little girl grows up, becomes tired of being a Goblin Queen and finds a human child and passes the Throne onto them, they gain the Goblin Queen condition. Resolving the Condition the former Goblin Queen becomes a Changeling with Goblin debt 9, having spent no time in Arcadia at all and possible no Kith.<br /> <br /> Also what is the Wyrd stat/contracts of the formily human Goblin Queen? <br /> <br /> I would think if they inherited all your subjects, they'd have to gain equal Wyrd to your wyrd at that time. <br /> <br /> So if you have 10 Wyrd which means 10 loyal subjects, then the child would gain 10 Wyrd upon becoming a Goblin Queen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","user":"Omegaphallic","date":". 04-01-2017, 10:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-01T19:45:57-07:00","id":1071874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1071445-goblin-contract-preview?p=1071869#post1071869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just came back from seeing Power Rangers, and I just realized:<br /> <br /> The Debt system is an excellent way to RP becoming a Sentai or Magical Girls villain.<br /> <br /> Seriously, you have the Goblin Queen who cannot fight the heroes directly that often, her loyal, Condition-mandated lieutenants, and the various goblins she trawls up from the Hedge as the monsters of the week. There's even a system for calling them into being if the Queen figures out how to birth Incubi from the dreams of her victims. <br /> <br /> Going away from my April Fool's mandated idea, does anyone want to play a game where all the players are Goblin Monarchs? Sort of like an alliance between them to form a sort of Hedge Empire and attempt to conquer/liberate/whatever a city?</div> </div> </div> </div> Once the game is released so we have more details that would be a cool idea.<br /> <br /> Then the challenge becomes how to keep everyone from being Jareth <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> An interesting twist to your idea could be that these Goblin Monarchs were a Motley that barely survived the collapse of a Freehold. As everyone else was lost, the Motley drew heavily upon Goblin Contracts while keeping the huntsmen at bay.<br /> <br /> Then they used Reaping to finish becoming Goblin Queens, so as to throw the huntsman off.<br /> <br /> So now they are trying to reclaim the city from the True Fae and their huntsmen servants, while manipulating newly Free Changelings into rebuilding the Freehold.<br /> <br /> I can see 3 reasons for a Changeling to become a Goblin Queen on purpose. <br /> <br /> 1. To get rid of a persistent huntsmen on their trail. <br /> 2. To transcend being a Changeling, but remain free of the Gentry.<br /> 3. So you can pass it onto a mortal child, maybe for some reason you need the child to be something other then human","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","user":"Omegaphallic","date":". 04-01-2017, 11:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-01T20:09:35-07:00","id":1071879,"title":"","content":"Unless a Character wants to become a goblin queen, what advantage does Goblin contracts hold over Court and Arcadian contracts, why would changelings turn to goblin contracts over Arcadian or Court Contracts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-01T20:53:54-07:00","id":1071888,"title":"","content":"I haven't read anything from David in a bit. He's still developing the line, right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-01T20:59:16-07:00","id":1071890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1071445-goblin-contract-preview?p=1071888#post1071888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I haven't read anything from David in a bit. He's still developing the line, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u2026<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1060128-david-hill-has-left-opp-what-happens-to-changeling-now-changeling-is-still-happening\">No</a>? Monghani linked straight to the content, but <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/goblin-contracts-changeling-the-lost/\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> is the blog post that the preview was introduced in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-01T22:10:46-07:00","id":1071911,"title":"","content":"Oh, boo - I mean I trust Rose, but I'm sad to see David go.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-01T22:23:17-07:00","id":1071917,"title":"","content":"EDIT: Actually, nope, not kicking that again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-01T22:37:04-07:00","id":1071922,"title":"","content":"Quick question for <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2\" data-vbnamecard=\"2\">Rose Bailey</a> or anyone else who knows and is allowed to say. Hedge Denizen and Goblin Queen are listed as Persistent Conditions. What are their Beat criteria?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 04-02-2017, 01:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-01T22:50:15-07:00","id":1071926,"title":"","content":"Am I the only one who thinks Goblin Debt should be a Condition as well? Write it as &quot;Goblin Debt X&quot;, just like you do with Tempted in Requiem. The effect of the Condition could be the Storyteller trading Debt for dice penalties as per the preview doc, and trading Debt for Conditions and Tilts can be the Beat criteria, and the Resolution criteria could be having X Reach reach 10 and voluntarily taking Hedge Denizen. Having X reach 0 could remove the Condition without Resolving it. This puts the decision to trade accumulated Debt for Conditions in the player's hands, thereby circumventing <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7212_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7212\" data-vbnamecard=\"7212\">Vent0</a>'s concern about vindictive STs, as well as being more in keeping with 2e's carrots over sticks philosophy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 04-02-2017, 01:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-02T04:29:06-07:00","id":1071978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1071445-goblin-contract-preview?p=1071879#post1071879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless a Character wants to become a goblin queen, what advantage does Goblin contracts hold over Court and Arcadian contracts, why would changelings turn to goblin contracts over Arcadian or Court Contracts?</div> </div> </div> </div> Court Contracts, I imagine, require epic feats of skill and cunning to acomplish striking the deal. And I don't think that Arcadian Contracts can really be casually made by changelings either. So, Goblin Contracts can do things changelings won't be able to make on their own without, well, making an entire Court system and all the details and requirements that entails.<br /> <br /> Goblin Contracts, for instance, are the only way I know how to manipulate one's Mantle and change its appearance without making an entirely new Contract, and, as I said above, making new Contracts is not as simple as, say, a vampire making a new Devotion or a werewolf making a fetish that alters a facet. Going by lore outside of Equinox Roads, making new Contracts is HARD. If that stays true in 2e, then that gives very compelling reason for Goblin Contracts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1071445-goblin-contract-preview?p=1071922#post1071922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Quick question for <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2\" data-vbnamecard=\"2\">Rose Bailey</a> or anyone else who knows and is allowed to say. Hedge Denizen and Goblin Queen are listed as Persistent Conditions. What are their Beat criteria?</div> </div> </div> </div> Its possible that they just don't have Beat criteria. There's plenty of core book Persistent Conditions with only Resolutions and no Beats beyond that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1071445-goblin-contract-preview?p=1071926#post1071926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Am I the only one who thinks Goblin Debt should be a Condition as well? Write it as &quot;Goblin Debt X&quot;, just like you do with Tempted in Requiem. The effect of the Condition could be the Storyteller trading Debt for dice penalties as per the preview doc, and trading Debt for Conditions and Tilts can be the Beat criteria, and the Resolution criteria could be having X Reach reach 10 and voluntarily taking Hedge Denizen. Having X reach 0 could remove the Condition without Resolving it. This puts the decision to trade accumulated Debt for Conditions in the player's hands, thereby circumventing <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7212_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7212\" data-vbnamecard=\"7212\">Vent0</a>'s concern about vindictive STs, as well as being more in keeping with 2e's carrots over sticks philosophy.</div> </div> </div> </div> Now, I'm going to be one of the first to advocate for there should be some way for PCs to pay off debt when they have the chance. Its very odd to have a debt you can't pay off. That'd be like me going to a credit card company and have them refuse payments to pay off my bill because they want to drag me into bankrupcy for some reason. Makes no sense to me, either from a logcal standpoint, or from a story standpoint. People want their payment.<br /> <br /> That said, by making it a Condition, it also leaves it entirely in the hands of a player, when there should be some input by the ST on when the metaphorical debt collectors / bookie thugs show up and extract payment by force. People want their payment. Conditions are entirely in the hands of the players, and I feel that there needs to be some input on both sides here - the debtor and the collector.<br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT - perhaps by paying both the glamour and the Loophole?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 04-02-2017, 08:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-02T05:03:41-07:00","id":1071984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1071445-goblin-contract-preview?p=1071926#post1071926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Am I the only one who thinks Goblin Debt should be a Condition as well? Write it as &quot;Goblin Debt X&quot;, just like you do with Tempted in Requiem. The effect of the Condition could be the Storyteller trading Debt for dice penalties as per the preview doc, and trading Debt for Conditions and Tilts can be the Beat criteria, and the Resolution criteria could be having X Reach reach 10 and voluntarily taking Hedge Denizen. Having X reach 0 could remove the Condition without Resolving it. This puts the decision to trade accumulated Debt for Conditions in the player's hands, thereby circumventing <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7212_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7212\" data-vbnamecard=\"7212\">Vent0</a>'s concern about vindictive STs, as well as being more in keeping with 2e's carrots over sticks philosophy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait, <i>my</i> concern? I thought that was <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5803_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5803\" data-vbnamecard=\"5803\">Taidragon</a>'s?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-02T05:48:12-07:00","id":1071988,"title":"","content":"How restrictive is Goblin Fate? From the wording, it feels like it can only be used to win money or in a Chase. Is that correct, or is it more flexible than that? Could it be used to, say, guess what cup held poison in a game to the death with a Sicilian? <br /> <br /> Given the existance of the Gambler's Cat, what advantage does this offer outside of a Chase to someone with both?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-02T06:19:08-07:00","id":1071994,"title":"","content":"Anyone else noticed the section called Collectors was reacted? <br /> <br /> That could be interesting. <br /> <br /> I'll also say Goblin Queens kind of make new factions within Freeholds beyond the Courts, after all you might not really be a court member anymore, at least until your condition is resolved but your still a member of the Freehold.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-02T06:20:44-07:00","id":1071996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1071445-goblin-contract-preview?p=1071984#post1071984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wait, <i>my</i> concern? I thought that was <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span>'s?</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh. Yeah, it was, I misread. That's what I get for posting at midnight, I guess.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-02T06:25:55-07:00","id":1071997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1071445-goblin-contract-preview?p=1071978#post1071978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Court Contracts, I imagine, require epic feats of skill and cunning to acomplish striking the deal. And I don't think that Arcadian Contracts can really be casually made by changelings either. So, Goblin Contracts can do things changelings won't be able to make on their own without, well, making an entire Court system and all the details and requirements that entails.<br /> <br /> Goblin Contracts, for instance, are the only way I know how to manipulate one's Mantle and change its appearance without making an entirely new Contract, and, as I said above, making new Contracts is not as simple as, say, a vampire making a new Devotion or a werewolf making a fetish that alters a facet. Going by lore outside of Equinox Roads, making new Contracts is HARD. If that stays true in 2e, then that gives very compelling reason for Goblin Contracts.<br /> <br /> Its possible that they just don't have Beat criteria. There's plenty of core book Persistent Conditions with only Resolutions and no Beats beyond that.<br /> <br /> Now, I'm going to be one of the first to advocate for there should be some way for PCs to pay off debt when they have the chance. Its very odd to have a debt you can't pay off. That'd be like me going to a credit card company and have them refuse payments to pay off my bill because they want to drag me into bankrupcy for some reason. Makes no sense to me, either from a logcal standpoint, or from a story standpoint. People want their payment.<br /> <br /> That said, by making it a Condition, it also leaves it entirely in the hands of a player, when there should be some input by the ST on when the metaphorical debt collectors / bookie thugs show up and extract payment by force. People want their payment. Conditions are entirely in the hands of the players, and I feel that there needs to be some input on both sides here - the debtor and the collector.<br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT - perhaps by paying both the glamour and the Loophole?</div> </div> </div> </div> So the idea is that Goblin Contracts can be established more on the fly, easier, but at the cost of incurring goblin debt to use, the price to be payed for taking a short cut to creating contracts as it were. <br /> <br /> I wonder if Goblin debt will be added to Goblin Vows.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-02T06:30:14-07:00","id":1071998,"title":"","content":"Speculation on my part, but I think Pupil's Dedication will be a merit where you can learn Arcadian contracts outside of your Regalia at reduced cost if you have a teacher who knows the contract.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-02T06:32:57-07:00","id":1071999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1071445-goblin-contract-preview?p=1071978#post1071978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Its possible that they just don't have Beat criteria. There's plenty of core book Persistent Conditions with only Resolutions and no Beats beyond that.</div> </div> </div> </div>No there aren't. The core book formatted its Conditions differently than every other Chronicles of Darkness book, writing their Beat criteria under the Resolution criteria instead of on a separate line, and including separate instructions for how the Condition can be &quot;shed&quot;. Presumably to save a little space, under the logic that when you Resolve a Condition you gain a Beat, and Persistent Conditions are not easily removed, so Resolving them should be different than &quot;shedding&quot; them. However, if you look at the exact same Persistent Conditions in any other book, all of them have Beat criteria. That's the only difference between Conditions and Persistent Conditions; Persistent Conditions have Beat criteria, other Conditions don't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-02T07:12:19-07:00","id":1072008,"title":"","content":"I could see granting a beat for Hedge Denizen every time the condition isolates you from Changeling society. <br /> <br /> For Goblin Queens every time a character is unable to act, because they are out of their allotted Ironside, get a beat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-02T08:08:40-07:00","id":1072020,"title":"","content":"I very like general idea of Goblin Contracts - only the proposed Debt limits seems to much to work for vindictive/careless ST, like in this scenario:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1071445-goblin-contract-preview?p=1071854#post1071854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And to be fair, a player who hits 10 Debt is going to do so expecting either 1) to hit Hedge Denizen, or 2) to get smacked with a large debt on purpose because of plot hooks.</div> </div> </div> </div>But one the other hand, limit of 5 Debt per level seems rather big to let PCs slide in to 'Goblinhood' on not repaying their Debts.<br /> <br /> Myself, I would go with this Debts limits:<ul><li><b>3 Debt</b> for Condition or Tilt - Most of Conditions already do something like +/- 2 to rolls, seems appropiate price for making something more out of those penalties.</li> <li><b>6 Debt</b> for Persistent Condition - Seems much more 'story showing' than only at Debt 10 like in document as now.</li> <li><b>9 Debt</b> for becoming Hedge Denize (or 'gobilinization' <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ) - Waiting 3 levels let to make players much more belief in 'Oh, I totally can get one more Debt and do not become Goblin' thing. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> And then those looking FOR becoming Goblin Queens will need to watch out more for getting Conditions by the way. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></li> </ul><br /> And truly beuty of this is that 'gobilization', now it's 1 Debt level<i> less </i>than document states it. And also we have in-game Rule of Three. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-02T09:02:34-07:00","id":1072040,"title":"","content":"I thought that Goblin Contracts were intended to be unique contracts created between (Or through) a goblin and the changeling? Is that not the case, or will be given guidelines for creating contracts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-02T09:21:23-07:00","id":1072045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1071445-goblin-contract-preview?p=1071999#post1071999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No there aren't. The core book formatted its Conditions differently than every other Chronicles of Darkness book, writing their Beat criteria under the Resolution criteria instead of on a separate line, and including separate instructions for how the Condition can be &quot;shed&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div> And those generally revolve around &quot;suffer trouble or a setback as a result of the Condition.&quot; As things stand, you're suffering the drawback as a matter of course - loss of Court and all that implies - without a beat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-02T09:23:14-07:00","id":1072046,"title":"","content":"I like (and am suitably horrified, I think) that overuse of Goblin Contracts leads to the character themselves <i>becoming</i> a Goblin, but that it is more a Condition than anything else. Kind of makes me wonder exactly <i>what</i> Hobgoblins are in this edition of Changeling if a regular Goblin is a Changeling (or possibly Fae-Touched, if they can buy Goblin Contracts) warped by their debt into something inhuman. Goblin Queens I find a fascinating concept, because it allows for a third faction of the Lost besides Courtiers and Loyalists that fits the conceptual space that 'low-Morality/Clarity' Hedge dwelling Changelings did back in First Edition. It also makes me think of the whole Seelie/Unseelie divide, as well as the Solitary/Trooping divide.<br /> <br /> Changeling 2E is digging deep into faerie lore and I am <i>loving </i>it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-02T09:28:23-07:00","id":1072048,"title":"","content":"I'm glad that Seeming benefits on contracts is still a thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-02T09:41:32-07:00","id":1072057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1071445-goblin-contract-preview?p=1072046#post1072046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Goblin Queens I find a fascinating concept, because it allows for a third faction of the Lost besides Courtiers and Loyalists that fits the conceptual space that 'low-Morality/Clarity' Hedge dwelling Changelings did back in First Edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Goblin Queens start to work in my head as go to for 'Powerfull Fae from myths' reinterpretation...<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/mTiy6Qp.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/BD9SWJW.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/1jG9Cfo.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Pfff, who needs True Fae when we have scenes like that! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 04-02-2017, 01:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-02T10:04:33-07:00","id":1072067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1071445-goblin-contract-preview?p=1072046#post1072046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like (and am suitably horrified, I think) that overuse of Goblin Contracts leads to the character themselves <i>becoming</i> a Goblin, but that it is more a Condition than anything else. Kind of makes me wonder exactly <i>what</i> Hobgoblins are in this edition of Changeling if a regular Goblin is a Changeling (or possibly Fae-Touched, if they can buy Goblin Contracts) warped by their debt into something inhuman. Goblin Queens I find a fascinating concept, because it allows for a third faction of the Lost besides Courtiers and Loyalists that fits the conceptual space that 'low-Morality/Clarity' Hedge dwelling Changelings did back in First Edition. It also makes me think of the whole Seelie/Unseelie divide, as well as the Solitary/Trooping divide.<br /> <br /> Changeling 2E is digging deep into faerie lore and I am <i>loving </i>it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, I think that they've already explained that goblins refers to &quot;anyone who treats the Hedge as their home.&quot; It's more of a descriptor than a category (&quot;That's Mike, he became a goblin when he realized he could think more like the living if his anchors were moved here&quot;), but given how the Hedge is all defined by the same laws, they're also all part of the same genus and resemble each other in type of power.<br /> <br /> Beyond that, the Hedge is actually a very generous landlord. Arcadian emigrants, exiled humans, Dreams who gained a mind of their own, mobile plantlife, changeling-goblins, Hobs...the Hedge has a citizenry that is much of a phatasmagoric hodgepodge as it is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-02T10:33:20-07:00","id":1072084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1071445-goblin-contract-preview?p=1072067#post1072067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually, I think that they've already explained that goblins refers to &quot;anyone who treats the Hedge as their home.&quot; It's more of a descriptor than a category (&quot;That's Mike, he became a goblin when he realized he could think more like the living if his anchors were moved here&quot;), but given how the Hedge is all defined by the same laws, they're also all part of the same genus and resemble each other in type of power.<br /> <br /> Beyond that, the Hedge is actually a very generous landlord. Arcadian emigrants, exiled humans, Dreams who gained a mind of their own, mobile plantlife, changeling-goblins, Hobs...the Hedge has a citizenry that is much of a phatasmagoric hodgepodge as it is.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it reflects well with the lore of Japanese yokai being Eastern fae creatures. Yokai include spirits of the dead, living and dead animal spirits, demons, oni, and so on. It certainly seems like a diverse category to my Western eyes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10118-bronzedog","name":"BronzeDog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-02T12:10:35-07:00","id":1072127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1071445-goblin-contract-preview?p=1072045#post1072045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> And those generally revolve around &quot;suffer trouble or a setback as a result of the Condition.&quot; As things stand, you're suffering the drawback as a matter of course - loss of Court and all that implies - without a beat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly, which means they should either give you Beats for the drawback you are suffering, or not be labeled Persistent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-02T12:13:51-07:00","id":1072129,"title":"","content":"I absolutely adore Goblin Queen by the way, and would love either to play one or to use one as an ally or antagonist in a game I run.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-02T12:44:12-07:00","id":1072137,"title":"","content":"Perhaps it should be renamed Goblin Monarch, just an idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-02T12:47:16-07:00","id":1072138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1071445-goblin-contract-preview?p=1072137#post1072137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps it should be renamed Goblin Monarch, just an idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I want to be Goblin King, too! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-02T13:02:41-07:00","id":1072142,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1071445-goblin-contract-preview?p=1072137#post1072137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps it should be renamed Goblin Monarch, just an idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>But just think of the wonderful , potentially awkward scenes where a male Goblin Queen has to explain the term is gender neutral.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-02T13:04:12-07:00","id":1072144,"title":"","content":"Eh. Traditionally-male titles get used as the default for title holders of any gender often enough (see &quot;Prince&quot; for vampires, for example). It's refreshing to see the opposite now and then.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-02T14:14:16-07:00","id":1072174,"title":"","content":"In the Toronto setting the leader of the freehold is the Scheherazade and styled Sultana no matter what their actual gender!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10769-llegume","name":"LLegume","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-02T14:19:12-07:00","id":1072182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1071445-goblin-contract-preview?p=1072144#post1072144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh. Traditionally-male titles get used as the default for title holders of any gender often enough (see &quot;Prince&quot; for vampires, for example). It's refreshing to see the opposite now and then.</div> </div> </div> </div>In play, we still will be generally using Gender Appropriate form - even most open STs just goes in standard names and terms until players will not mark things like that as problem, just to cut communication issues.<br /> <br /> To be fair, even in my <b>Masquerade</b> game ( for 3 months ) 15 years ago, we used term Princes for female vampiric rulers of city.<br /> <br /> And Monarch is Gender Neutral, as goes for English. ( Or at least as far I know language. )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-02T14:29:25-07:00","id":1072190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1071445-goblin-contract-preview?p=1072182#post1072182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In play, we still will be generally using Gender Appropriate form - even most open STs just goes in standard names and terms until players will not mark things like that as problem, just to cut communication issues.<br /> <br /> To be fair, even in my <b>Masquerade</b> game ( for 3 months ) 15 years ago, we used term Princes for female vampiric rulers of city.</div> </div> </div> </div>That makes sense. And there's no reason you couldn't do the same with male characters who gain the Goblin Queen Condition.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1071445-goblin-contract-preview?p=1072182#post1072182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And Monarch is Gender Neutral, as goes for English. ( Or at least as far I know language. )</div> </div> </div> </div>It is, I just think Goblin Queen sounds cooler, and it seems like a double standard to be worried about the default name for the Condition being gender-neutral when no such concern is forthcoming about the default title for vampire leaders.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-02T14:56:46-07:00","id":1072201,"title":"","content":"Prince was originally more generic in English. The Prince was once just the ruler of a (small) state, regardless of gender (I think Queen Elizabeth I was sometimes called a prince). Vampire draws from Machiavelli, rather than our modern term for &quot;son of the king&quot;.<br /> <br /> Edit: or rather, it wasn't explicitly masculine in the way we think of it now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":". 04-02-2017, 06:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-02T15:05:51-07:00","id":1072205,"title":"","content":"I am 100% in favour of it remaining Goblin Queen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-02T15:13:40-07:00","id":1072208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1071445-goblin-contract-preview?p=1072201#post1072201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Prince was originally more generic in English. The Prince was once just the ruler of a (small) state, regardless of gender (I think Queen Elizabeth I was sometimes called a prince). Vampire draws from Machiavelli, rather than our modern term for &quot;son of the king&quot;.<br /> <br /> Edit: or rather, it wasn't explicitly masculine in the way we think of it now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, but of the people who have not protested the term's non-gender-neutrality, how many do you think follow this reasoning for their lack of protest? I would be willing to bet less than half.<br /> <br /> Like, even if there's historical prescedent for male-centric terms being used gender-neutrally, it's still a double-standard to protest female-centric terms being used gender-neutrally and not to make the same protestations about the male-centric terms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 04-02-2017, 06:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-02T15:50:15-07:00","id":1072224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1071445-goblin-contract-preview?p=1072208#post1072208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sure, but of the people who have not protested the term's non-gender-neutrality, how many do you think follow this reasoning for their lack of protest? I would be willing to bet less than half.<br /> <br /> Like, even if there's historical prescedent for male-centric terms being used gender-neutrally, it's still a double-standard to protest female-centric terms being used gender-neutrally and not to make the same protestations about the male-centric terms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh no, I totally agree. I was just historical factoiding.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-02T17:22:28-07:00","id":1072257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LLegume</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1071445-goblin-contract-preview?p=1072174#post1072174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the Toronto setting the leader of the freehold is the Scheherazade and styled Sultana no matter what their actual gender!</div> </div> </div> </div> I'm fine with the Sultana title, because the writing makes it clear why its Sultana no matter what the gender of the person holding the office, its intended as an homage to the first Sultana of the freehold, the person who holds the office isn't just a politician, they treated like an incarnation of the first Sultina, continuing the cycle of story telling that keeps the Freehold safe. <br /> <br /> And my concern isn't just about gender, it's also about culture, a Russian Goblin Queen might prefer Czar/Czarina, a Arabian might prefer Caliph, an Epyptian Pharoah, an American might prefer Goblin President.<br /> <br /> I'm actually fine with using Queen gender nuetrally if that's what people want, although others may have issues, with it, it was just a suggestion that might improve marketing. It's no skin off my back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","user":"Omegaphallic","date":". 04-02-2017, 08:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-02T17:38:57-07:00","id":1072263,"title":"","content":"I wonder if Regalia has any effect on a changeling's me in? <br /> <br /> And does Regalia have an mechanical effect beyond Arcadian Contract costs. <br /> <br /> And am I the only one who wonders what happens to a former Goblin Queen who started out human instead of Changeling when they finally resolve the condition. I mean by raw they become a Changeling, but how do they deal with Seeming and Kith on a Changeling who never visited Arcadia?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-02T17:40:03-07:00","id":1072265,"title":"","content":"It just occurred to me; changelings are now the most likely post-human supernatural creature to step outside their liminality. They can 'ascend' to True Fae, become and remain a Goblin, or even become human once again. Only Beasts rival them in how available and easy their methods of transcendence are, and I recall one of the themes the two share is dreams. Like a midsummer night's dream, perhaps.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-02T17:42:35-07:00","id":1072267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1071445-goblin-contract-preview?p=1072263#post1072263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if Regalia has any effect on a changeling's me in? <br /> <br /> And does Regalia have an mechanical effect beyond Arcadian Contract costs. <br /> <br /> And am I the only one who wonders what happens to a former Goblin Queen who started out human instead of Changeling when they finally resolve the condition. I mean by raw they become a Changeling, but how do they deal with Seeming and Kith on a Changeling who never visited Arcadia?</div> </div> </div> </div>If humans becoming changelings indirectly through inheriting and shedding Goblin Queenhood isn't an editing miss... I'd say they inherit the Kith of the changeling who enthroned them. Seeming could reflect how and why they shed Queenhood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-02T18:00:33-07:00","id":1072274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1071445-goblin-contract-preview?p=1072265#post1072265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It just occurred to me; changelings are now the most likely post-human supernatural creature to step outside their liminality. They can 'ascend' to True Fae, become and remain a Goblin, or even become human once again. Only Beasts rival them in how available and easy their methods of transcendence are, and I recall one of the themes the two share is dreams. Like a midsummer night's dream, perhaps.</div> </div> </div> </div> I'd add achieving Wyrd 10 to that, because at that point they become immortal and powerful enough that even the Gentry take them seriously. <br /> <br /> Seriously even Master Mages and Demons would have second thoughts about going toe to toe with a Wyrd 10 Changeling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-02T18:04:49-07:00","id":1072277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1071445-goblin-contract-preview?p=1072267#post1072267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If humans becoming changelings indirectly through inheriting and shedding Goblin Queenhood isn't an editing miss... I'd say they inherit the Kith of the changeling who enthroned them. Seeming could reflect how and why they shed Queenhood.</div> </div> </div> </div> Makes sense to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-02T18:14:33-07:00","id":1072280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1071445-goblin-contract-preview?p=1072274#post1072274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd add achieving Wyrd 10 to that, because at that point they become immortal and powerful enough that even the Gentry take them seriously. <br /> <br /> Seriously even Master Mages and Demons would have second thoughts about going toe to toe with a Wyrd 10 Changeling.</div> </div> </div> </div>I meant transcendence as in becoming something else, rather than becoming something powerful...<br /> <br /> But yeah, still agree with you on Wyrd 10 changelings being a force of nature.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-02T18:55:59-07:00","id":1072298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1071445-goblin-contract-preview?p=1072190#post1072190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That makes sense. And there's no reason you couldn't do the same with male characters who gain the Goblin Queen Condition.<br /> <br /> <br /> It is, I just think Goblin Queen sounds cooler, and it seems like a double standard to be worried about the default name for the Condition being gender-neutral when no such concern is forthcoming about the default title for vampire leaders.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Honestly, it sounds incongrous to gender-locked old me...but I can think of an interesting history behind &quot;Queen&quot; being the unigender title;<br /> <br /> I'd say that term came soon after eusociality was fully discovered, when the Lost did a full study of Goblin Queens. It was originally thought that all of their direct minions were Oneiroi born from the Queens themselves. In effect, they were the &quot;mothers&quot; of their minions, more like the reigning mother of a hive than a true regent.<br /> <br /> Of course, this was also around the point where the dominant Lost culture was based around a grand phobia of insanity and prejudice against those who were dealing with Clarity issues. Those were the days of the hippie movement, something that quickly earned the suspicions of changelings when it turns out hippie behavior tends to induce breaking points. As a result, anything that resembled the New Age was regarded as inherently suspect and likely enthralled by the True Fae. Thus, the Hedge was regarded as far more of a trap than it actually is, and all hobgoblins unknowing minions-so, of course, the fact that some changelings not only adapted to it, but so well that the Huntsman can no longer find them, was a bit of cognitive dissonance that could only be solved by largely pretending that Goblin Queens who willingly agreed to oaths of non-betrayal were not, somehow, goblins.<br /> <br /> As the Red Scare and hippies passed by, most Lost realized how stupid this was, but the name stuck. <br /> <br /> (It should be noted that birthing Oneiroi for a set of minions is entirely possible, it's just not always how a Queen gains her court).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-02T19:00:06-07:00","id":1072301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1071445-goblin-contract-preview?p=1072257#post1072257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm fine with the Sultana title, because the writing makes it clear why its Sultana no matter what the gender of the person holding the office, its intended as an homage to the first Sultana of the freehold, the person who holds the office isn't just a politician, they treated like an incarnation of the first Sultina, continuing the cycle of story telling that keeps the Freehold safe.<br /> <br /> And my concern isn't just about gender, it's also about culture, a Russian Goblin Queen might prefer Czar/Czarina, a Arabian might prefer Caliph, an Epyptian Pharoah, an American might prefer Goblin President.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, for sure. I don't doubt there would be local variations. I mean, who even knows if they would call themselves anything; Goblin Queen is just the name of the Condition, from what we know they may or may not hold any actual power over goblins. In fact, since it's acquired by accumulating unpaid debt, it seems more like a service position than a position of power. The name is more likely just a not-so-subtle Labyrinth reference than meant to indicate actual monarchy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-02T19:05:29-07:00","id":1072303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1071445-goblin-contract-preview?p=1072298#post1072298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, it sounds incongrous to gender-locked old me...</div> </div> </div> </div>Please don't take this the wrong way, but the fact that it ill-fits your culturally-ingrained preconceptions about gender doesn't change the fact that it's a double-standard. It just indicates that the double-standard exists on a deep cultural level rather than on an individual level.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-02T19:21:34-07:00","id":1072309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1071445-goblin-contract-preview?p=1072263#post1072263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if Regalia has any effect on a changeling's me in?<br /> <br /> And does Regalia have an mechanical effect beyond Arcadian Contract costs.<br /> <br /> And am I the only one who wonders what happens to a former Goblin Queen who started out human instead of Changeling when they finally resolve the condition. I mean by raw they become a Changeling, but how do they deal with Seeming and Kith on a Changeling who never visited Arcadia?</div> </div> </div> </div>There are a few possible answers here. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12619_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12619\" data-vbnamecard=\"12619\">21C Hermit</a> already brought up the possibilities of it being an oversight and of the human gaining the Queen's Seeming and Kith. Other possibilities I can think of: Replacing the Goblin Queen acts as a Durance despite not technically being in Arcadia; their Kith is based on what their role as Goblin Queen was (likely something related to royalty), and their Seeming is based on how they got out of being the Queen (Darkling seems likely, since the Resolution for Goblin Queen typically entails finding another human to replace yourself with). Alternatively, since they were never in Arcadia they cannot become Changelings, but since they were in the Hedge, they come back as Fae-Touched. No Kith, Seeming either related to the Seeming of the previous Queen, the seeming of the Changeling that helped them escape (if any), or Unseemly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-02T19:56:25-07:00","id":1072325,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1071445-goblin-contract-preview?p=1072303#post1072303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Please don't take this the wrong way, but the fact that it ill-fits your culturally-ingrained preconceptions about gender doesn't change the fact that it's a double-standard. It just indicates that the double-standard exists on a deep cultural level rather than on an individual level.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Um, yes?<br /> <br /> That was what I was implying.<br /> <br /> I said that to be self-effectuating. &quot;I know this is based on a stupid reason, but it still hits my ears wrong, so I'm making a story as to why people thought it fit in universe, despite several centuries of gendering making it so that female titles are almost never unigender that likely does not matter, but explores a bit of Lost culture.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","user":"Leliel","date":". 04-02-2017, 10:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-02T20:34:07-07:00","id":1072340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1071445-goblin-contract-preview?p=1072325#post1072325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Um, yes?<br /> <br /> That was what I was implying.<br /> <br /> I said that to be self-effectuating. &amp;quot;I know this is based on a stupid reason, but it still hits my ears wrong, so I'm making a story as to why people thought it fit in universe, despite several centuries of gendering making it so that female titles are almost never unigender that likely does not matter, but explores a bit of Lost culture.&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Ahh, I got you now. Sorry for misunderstanding.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-03T02:58:25-07:00","id":1072423,"title":"","content":"This is only a factoid relating to eusociality, and not an argument to changing the name of the Condition (I agree with Charlaquin):<br /> Until the 1660s (which is, in fact, quite recently considering how old beekeeping actually is) the Queen bee was referred to as King. It was assumed that the largest bee in the colony would be a King, and it wasn't until after scientists discovered that the King had ovaries that the King started to be referred to as Queen, and that took some time for most people to get used to (and for the information to spread).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-03T05:56:37-07:00","id":1072473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1071445-goblin-contract-preview?p=1072298#post1072298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Honestly, it sounds incongrous to gender-locked old me...but I can think of an interesting history behind &amp;quot;Queen&amp;quot; being the unigender title;<br /> <br /> I'd say that term came soon after eusociality was fully discovered, when the Lost did a full study of Goblin Queens. It was originally thought that all of their direct minions were Oneiroi born from the Queens themselves. In effect, they were the &amp;quot;mothers&amp;quot; of their minions, more like the reigning mother of a hive than a true regent.<br /> <br /> Of course, this was also around the point where the dominant Lost culture was based around a grand phobia of insanity and prejudice against those who were dealing with Clarity issues. Those were the days of the hippie movement, something that quickly earned the suspicions of changelings when it turns out hippie behavior tends to induce breaking points. As a result, anything that resembled the New Age was regarded as inherently suspect and likely enthralled by the True Fae. Thus, the Hedge was regarded as far more of a trap than it actually is, and all hobgoblins unknowing minions-so, of course, the fact that some changelings not only adapted to it, but so well that the Huntsman can no longer find them, was a bit of cognitive dissonance that could only be solved by largely pretending that Goblin Queens who willingly agreed to oaths of non-betrayal were not, somehow, goblins.<br /> <br /> As the Red Scare and hippies passed by, most Lost realized how stupid this was, but the name stuck. <br /> <br /> (It should be noted that birthing Oneiroi for a set of minions is entirely possible, it's just not always how a Queen gains her court).</div> </div> </div> </div> If the Goblin Queen creates their own minions then Queen makes sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-03T06:56:37-07:00","id":1072504,"title":"","content":"It may just be my love of Riddle-kith speaking, but an Elemental with Riddle-kith and Mantle-Mask (and the kith that means you don't need a disguise kit) would be...pretty damn dangerous in a freehold. They could literally be anyone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-03T09:48:25-07:00","id":1072580,"title":"","content":"If you're human and take the place of a goblin queen, you take on their seeming and kith.<br /> <br /> (I hadn't previously considered that it might change a Changeling's seeming, but I'm going to talk that over with Meghan and the team.)<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also this...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Liza Cantwell, Age 9, Goblin Queen</span></b><br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Kneel before the queen!&quot; [dissolves into giggles]</i><br /> <br /> <b>Background: </b>Liza's been in the Hedge about a year now, left here by someone who took so many Goblin Contracts and gathered so much Debt she became a Goblin Queen herself. In order to shed that Debt, she had to find a little girl to take her place. The woman tricked Liza into following her into the Hedge, then left her there to become the new Goblin Queen. Liza missed her parents at first, but when she gets sad, the pixies entertain her and make her laugh again. Sometimes they lead her on a chase, and the Thorns cut her. It probably should hurt, but it doesn't, really, and she doesn't feel so sad afterwards.<br /> <br /> <b>Description: </b>Liza is a nine-year-old little girl, wearing a finely made but very dirty dress. Changelings who have met Madam Thimblestitch might recognize her handiwork. She also wears a woven crown of flowers that is held in place by her tangled hair. Liza still carries her backpack, which contains her last few school assignments, a library book, and a handout about Stranger Danger.<br /> <br /> <b>Storytelling Hints: </b>For a kid who's spent a year as Goblin Queen, being fawned over by her faerie retainers, Liza is pretty even-keeled. She gives orders and expects them to be carried out, but she doesn't fly into rages or demand impossible things of her subjects. She can come across as a little cold, but she's lost a lot of herself to the Thorns. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":2,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","user":"Rose Bailey","date":". 04-03-2017, 03:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-03T12:00:54-07:00","id":1072638,"title":"","content":"I was going to say that the don't require a Seeming or a Kith. After all loyalist don't have Seeming. But Rose has already said otherwise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","name":"Blakemikizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-03T12:05:45-07:00","id":1072642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;<i><i>Liza missed her parents at first, but when she gets sad, the pixies entertain her and make her laugh again. Sometimes they lead her on a chase, and the Thorns cut her. It probably should hurt, but it doesn't, really, and she doesn't feel so sad afterwards.&quot;</i></i> </div> </div> </div>There is something really sad about it.<br /> <br /> Also, aren\u00b4t goblins supposed to be immune to the Thorns?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-03T12:17:25-07:00","id":1072649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1071445-goblin-contract-preview?p=1072642#post1072642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There is something really sad about it.<br /> <br /> Also, aren\u00b4t goblins supposed to be immune to the Thorns?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>They may or may not be. By definition, a Queen has a soul, and that can be cut if any goblin can be. That, and I don't think you acclimate to the Thorns instantly-Liza has a lot left to lose before she becomes a true goblin.<br /> <br /> Though, this does bring up an interesting hook: a Queen who abdicated her throne...and prompty built a new one to watch over the Princess, as the real intent was to save her heir from a terribad home.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-03T12:24:06-07:00","id":1072654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1071445-goblin-contract-preview?p=1072580#post1072580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you're human and take the place of a goblin queen, you take on their seeming and kith.<br /> <br /> (I hadn't previously considered that it might change a Changeling's seeming, but I'm going to talk that over with Meghan and the team.)<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also this...<br /></div> </div> </div> </div> I like the irony of her having a stranger danger pamphlet. <br /> <br /> And it's interesting that Human Goblin Queens that free themselves turn into Changelings with the previous Queen's Seeming and Kith. <br /> <br /> It allows Changelings to build lineages of a short from themselves. <br /> <br /> And it creates a demographic of Changelings that are very different then others, Changelings who were never in Arcadia, who have no Keeper. <br /> <br /> How do the Arcadia Changelings and Goblin Queen Changelings deal with each other? They're MASSIVE implications to the whole setting in this, as it created an entirely new class of Changeling, as well as making it possible for Changeling's to create new Changelings. <br /> <br /> I could see some Freeholds killing Goblin Queens on sight feeling their too much like the Gentry, other Freeholds could be entirely made up of former Goblin Queens, others might choose a Goblin Queen to rule the Freehold as they are separate from the court system, there for potentially Neutral, and others might see no real difference between the two. <br /> <br /> And if Fae Touched can use Goblin Contracts it gives them the ability to potentially become Changelings. <br /> <br /> I could see a desperate court using Goblin Queens to boost their populations.<br /> <br /> Massive implications. <br /> <br /> And if an Adult human wants to become a Goblin Queen, they could just get a Fae with the right contract and Seeming effect to da age them to childhood and have a Queen make them their successor.<br /> <br /> So for Human Fae hybrids you have Arcadian Changelings, Goblin Queen Changes, Cambions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","user":"Omegaphallic","date":". 04-03-2017, 03:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-03T12:35:00-07:00","id":1072657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1071445-goblin-contract-preview?p=1072649#post1072649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They may or may not be. By definition, a Queen has a soul, and that can be cut if any goblin can be. That, and I don't think you acclimate to the Thorns instantly-Liza has a lot left to lose before she becomes a true goblin.<br /> <br /> Though, this does bring up an interesting hook: a Queen who abdicated her throne...and prompty built a new one to watch over the Princess, as the real intent was to save her heir from a terribad home.</div> </div> </div> </div> Like I said huge implications.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-03T12:52:11-07:00","id":1072665,"title":"","content":"There's not a huge quantity of goblin social stuff in the core, but I'm very interested in it, and oh look there's that Hedge book on the schedule....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-03T12:56:53-07:00","id":1072669,"title":"","content":"A thing that's worth keeping in mind about different kinds of faerie creatures: the boundaries are not always firm. Each of the categories we as designers/players define have strong characteristics that distinguish them, but in practice, all sorts of weird exceptions and one-off events happen. So, for example, the circumstances of changelings and fae-touched and hobogblins are distinct from each other, but transitions and half-measures could happen in actual play.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Maybe I'll post the Ipswich, MA setting as one of the dev blogs. It nicely illustrates fae people who are a category of their own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-03T13:16:07-07:00","id":1072675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1071445-goblin-contract-preview?p=1072669#post1072669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A thing that's worth keeping in mind about different kinds of faerie creatures: the boundaries are not always firm. Each of the categories we as designers/players define have strong characteristics that distinguish them, but in practice, all sorts of weird exceptions and one-off events happen. So, for example, the circumstances of changelings and fae-touched and hobogblins are distinct from each other, but transitions and half-measures could happen in actual play.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Maybe I'll post the Ipswich, MA setting as one of the dev blogs. It nicely illustrates fae people who are a category of their own.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pleaseeeeeeeeeeee!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-03T14:22:50-07:00","id":1072698,"title":"","content":"Now what I find interesting is the fact that Children who became Goblin Queens don't have a Keeper gunning for them. They would have an whole different view of the True Fae that changelings don't. It adds a nice element to the game because you never know if a Goblin Queens in working with a Gentry.<br /> <br /> And every Goblin Queen has a reason to help a Huntsman to find the changeling that ruined their lives.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","name":"Blakemikizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-03T17:41:32-07:00","id":1072813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1071445-goblin-contract-preview?p=1072669#post1072669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A thing that's worth keeping in mind about different kinds of faerie creatures: the boundaries are not always firm. Each of the categories we as designers/players define have strong characteristics that distinguish them, but in practice, all sorts of weird exceptions and one-off events happen. So, for example, the circumstances of changelings and fae-touched and hobogblins are distinct from each other, but transitions and half-measures could happen in actual play.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Maybe I'll post the Ipswich, MA setting as one of the dev blogs. It nicely illustrates fae people who are a category of their own.</div> </div> </div> </div> Interesting, and there is a new setting in the Changeling or just a special dev blog post? <br /> <br /> I'm trying to think of all the categories and subcatogories of Fae. <br /> <br /> Oneiro (dream Fae like Succubi, Incubi, Cambions, Sandman), Hobs, Hedge Beasts (weirdly some over lap with Beasts from Beast the Primordial in some cases), Changelings, Goblins (including Goblin Queens), True Fae, Huntsmen, Fetchs, Fae Touched. <br /> <br /> Given that formerly human Goblin Queens become Changelings when cured, I'm guessing you just use the Changeling template for them, but make adjustments for the Goblin Queen condition. <br /> <br /> It also makes me wonder what types of Fae can join a Changeling Court or Freehold beyond Changelings and Fae Touched. I don't think Fetches can, but I could see a Cambion doing so, a Cambion might be considered an abomination, but they're still people, and their abilities would be an advantage for any Changeling court.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-03T17:42:34-07:00","id":1072814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1071445-goblin-contract-preview?p=1072675#post1072675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pleaseeeeeeeeeeee!</div> </div> </div> </div> I second this, it has me curious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-03T18:53:07-07:00","id":1072863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1071445-goblin-contract-preview?p=1072669#post1072669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A thing that's worth keeping in mind about different kinds of faerie creatures: the boundaries are not always firm. Each of the categories we as designers/players define have strong characteristics that distinguish them, but in practice, all sorts of weird exceptions and one-off events happen. So, for example, the circumstances of changelings and fae-touched and hobogblins are distinct from each other, but transitions and half-measures could happen in actual play.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Maybe I'll post the Ipswich, MA setting as one of the dev blogs. It nicely illustrates fae people who are a category of their own.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering a custom freehold I'm making actually has a fae-touched as the monarch of the newest court (and founder, if that's possible in the system we get), her goal ultimately being to actually become a Changeling so she can live long enough to not only free her husband but live a long life with him, reading that makes me very happy to hear. Heck, the Goblin Queen aspect alone already makes me very happy to read, because that's a legitimate avenue players could take in allowing her to become a Changeling (if an imperfect one).<br /> <br /> That said, I'm also wondering if there should be a custom Seeming for humans who take the place of a Changeling as Goblin Queen, who lost themselves to it but abdicated the throne (or had it stolen away) and regained some of their human self in turn. They didn't have a keeper, but in its place is something far more chaotic, a hunger for what they once had which haunts their dreams as much as any Changeling's. Because they are so vulgar a source, they don't typically pick up Seeming affinities, unless it ties into the Goblin Contracts/Debts in some way...<br /> <br /> Who knows? Maybe the reason the Huntsmen come around for them isn't so much because they're trying to bring these exiled Queens back to Arcadia (though perhaps as a token prize they could be taken), but because their former servants bribed a Huntsman to assist in finding the proper Changeling if said Huntsman helped them get their Queen back, for better or worse...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-03T23:34:09-07:00","id":1072966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1071445-goblin-contract-preview?p=1072863#post1072863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Heck, the Goblin Queen aspect alone already makes me very happy to read, because that's a legitimate avenue players could take in allowing her to become a Changeling (if an imperfect one).<br /> <br /> That said, I'm also wondering if there should be a custom Seeming for humans who take the place of a Changeling as Goblin Queen, who lost themselves to it but abdicated the throne (or had it stolen away) and regained some of their human self in turn. They didn't have a keeper, but in its place is something far more chaotic, a hunger for what they once had which haunts their dreams as much as any Changeling's. Because they are so vulgar a source, they don't typically pick up Seeming affinities, unless it ties into the Goblin Contracts/Debts in some way...</div> </div> </div> </div>Are not Grimms Seeming from Dark Eras about things like those?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-03T23:54:35-07:00","id":1072974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1071445-goblin-contract-preview?p=1072966#post1072966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Are not Grimms Seeming from Dark Eras about things like those?</div> </div> </div> </div>Grimms embraced the role they took in Arcadia in order to escape through the Hedge; I suppose they're somewhat like the Goblin-esc Seeming I proposed, but Grimms have to follow a particular role lest they become depressed, lose Clarity and easier to find from Huntsmen. That said, we haven't gotten any real notes on how they handle contracts, given there have been no Grimm Seeming affinities, even in the book they appeared in...unless I've completely missed that somewhere.<br /> <br /> The Goblin-Seeming was more an alternate option where Changelings have their worries closer to home, but said worries are less pressing (Goblins are hardly as great as the Gentry of Arcadia), and though they have no innate Seeming affinities with Arcadia contracts they'd have more luck with Goblin contracts...relatively speaking anyways. They weren't stolen to Arcadia, but were still stolen from reality, their lives bled from them by the thorns and the fact that they exist would be something of a sore point among Freeholds. A reminder that, yes, sometimes a Changeling can be just as selfish as a Gentry, and can ruin a normal life to make their own lives a bit easier. The more I think on it the less necessary it seem though, and the more it seems like fluff. Not sure, tis late, pondering a bit. The more I talk about it though, the less likely it is to be a thing due to copyright worries and all that.<br /> <br /> Still, it's a sign of how much I'm looking forwards to Changeling; I don't get ideas like this from properties that don't push at all the right buttons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T10:05:18-07:00","id":1073217,"title":"","content":"Just a weird thought, but can Goblin Queens offer goblin contracts to Changelings?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T11:12:56-07:00","id":1073261,"title":"","content":"Now isn't <i>that</i> a fun thought.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}